Vulkan: retire temporary wait semaphores, skip signaled imports, and bound acquire failures

Destroy per-command-buffer wait semaphores when their consuming submission
retires instead of pooling them until renderer teardown. Drivers such as NVIDIA
580.xx duplicate imported sync_file descriptors during vkImportSemaphoreFdKHR
and retain the internal FD until vkDestroySemaphore rather than closing it when
the queue wait completes, exhausting RLIMIT_NOFILE over long uptimes.

Also probe explicit wait timeline points and exported sync_file descriptors
before importing them into Vulkan semaphores so already-signaled dependencies
avoid temporary semaphore imports altogether, log FD table diagnostics at the
start of an acquire/import failure episode, and mark the renderer for
replacement after eight consecutive pre-submit acquire failures instead of
looping indefinitely without emitting events.lost.

